{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011368-supernatural-splats-as-drifters-squatters-in-cod","id":1011368,"title":"Supernatural splats as Drifters/Squatters in CoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-02T21:56:08-08:00","id":1011368,"title":"Supernatural splats as Drifters/Squatters in CoD","content":"So I wonder which supernatural splat has the easiest time or rather how the PCs would live as homeless drifters/hobos/squatters especially constantly on the move?<br /> <br /> Let's see now...<br /> <br /> I definatly see it naturally happen to Prometheans and Werewolves but I kinda wonder for Vampires, Changelings, Geists, Beasts, Mummies, etc and how can they be as such?<br /> <br /> Well the reason for this eversince I've watched &quot;Confessions of Fred Krueger&quot; where they used Freddy's original backstory envisioned by Wes Craven and Jeffery Cooper where he was a drifter/squatter before the whole &quot;Family Man&quot; angle was invented by Freddy's Dead where it was the worst of the series, I'm kinda inspired to making PCs in perhaps every supernatural splat to be drifters and avoiding the whole &quot;Family angle&quot; for them being husbands or wives nor have any interest of romance or marriage at all (which in Vampire's case, I wonder if they can avoid ghouling and blood bonding to achieve this for example?) just them living alone squatting in a abandoned factory, subway station, sewers or warehouse somewhere or maybe a entire group of PCs live there and are pretty communal and equal to each other with a little casual sex thrown here and there (instead of monogamous any type of romantic relationship) which is how I envision it (which I especially wonder if this is possible for Vampires and Changelings especially?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.co